PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H}

The question asks specifically for the *least* plausible explanation, given the historical context of the Bansenshukai (a 1676 compilation presented to the Tokugawa regime, with all surviving copies showing the same pattern of placeholder circles).  

H is the weakest by a wide margin. It fabricates an elaborate, ahistorical link between the Kuji-in, “nine holes,” Taoist sexual alchemy, and “erotic energy rituals” that has no documentary basis in any surviving ninja manual or in the known contents of the Bansenshukai itself. The other options, while varying in likelihood, at least rest on documented practices (redaction for security, moral censorship by Confucian-era copyists, physical wear of heavily consulted pages, or the use of aburidashi) or on verifiable historical actors and institutions (Oniwaban, Fujibayashi, Iga–Tokugawa ties). H, by contrast, is pure retrofitted esotericism and can be ruled out on that ground alone.

